│ ┃       Patch to Fix Sphinx Documentation for Methods with       ┃ │
│ ┃                   @classmethod and @property                   ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue arises because Sphinx does not document methods          │
│ decorated with both @classmethod and @property in Python 3.9+. The │
│ root cause is that the __doc__ attribute is inherited from the     │
│ wrapped descriptor, but Sphinx does not recognize this as a valid  │
│ documentation source for such methods.                             │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                            🛠️ Reasoning                             │
│                                                                    │
│ Sphinx's autodoc extension does not automatically document methods │
│ that are decorated with both @classmethod and @property when the   │
│ __doc__ attribute is inherited from the wrapped descriptor. This   │
│ is a known limitation in the current Sphinx version (4.0.3) and is │
│ expected to be resolved in Python 3.10. To address this, we need   │
│ to ensure that the __doc__ attribute is explicitly set for these   │
│ methods or adjust                                                  │
